import{_ as a,d as n,e as t,x as i}from"./chunks/framework.BRr8VP3a.js";const h=JSON.parse('{"title":"D.18 Money, Credit, Finance, and Crises","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"D.18 Money, Credit, Finance, and Crises","xkChars":0,"xkWords":463},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/theory/appendix-d/d-18.md","filePath":"en/theory/appendix-d/d-18.md"}'),s={name:"en/theory/appendix-d/d-18.md"};function o(r,e,d,c,l,p){return n(),t("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[i('<div class="theory-source"><h1 id="section-d-18" tabindex="-1"><span class="xk-num"><span class="xk-num__n">D.18</span><span class="xk-num__gap"></span></span>Money, Credit, Finance, and Crises <a class="header-anchor" href="#section-d-18" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;D.18 Money, Credit, Finance, and Crises {#section-d-18}&quot;">​</a></h1><p>In the main text, see §2.8, §6.6 and 6.12–6.13, §10.6.2, and §12. Research entries cover 18.01–18.11.</p><p>Financial analysis must retain currency, maturity, priority, security, the parties involved, and the basis of valuation. A loan creates an asset and a corresponding liability. This does not amount to an equal increase in net wealth. Writing off an asset does not automatically erase another party’s deposit. Insufficient cash flow, impaired net worth, frozen financing channels, and legal payment requirements are distinct conditions. “Overload” cannot stand in for all of them.</p><p>Maturity transformation can support investment and liquidity. Runs can involve coordination risk and fundamental risk. Keynes’s account of demand and uncertainty, theories of money and expectations, Minsky’s financing structures, debt deflation and the financial accelerator, and behavioral and narrative research offer different conditional explanations. Together they do not establish an inevitable crisis cycle.</p><p>In a teaching example, collateral value falls from 100 to 80 on a loan of 60 with a maximum loan-to-value ratio of 70%. The permitted balance falls to 56, creating a need to make up 4. This does not establish a loss of 4. If a fire sale brings in only 45, the remaining repayment and loss are a separate accounting question. Collateral revaluation, top-up payments, sale, price feedback, and contraction of lending must each be explained. A fall in price alone cannot supply the entire chain.</p><p>Account separately for the amount authorized for a rescue, the amount actually paid out, risk bearing in advance, and the final net cost. A temporary liquidity bridge can be useful without establishing that the capital position or long-term business model has been repaired. An average household debt-service ratio cannot substitute for the high-burden tail. Essential expenses and buffers must also be examined. Record links among different versions, analyses of the same plan, and reanalyses of the same data. Do not count independent evidence by the number of papers.</p><p>The same quarter can have different values under different methods or releases. Joining one point under the old method to the next under the new method can create a change absent from a series using the same version throughout. Restore a common method or defensible bridge before explaining the mechanism. Contractual payments, actual payments, changes in balances, and cash pressure require separate evidence. Revising a version does not establish households’ actual burdens or a policy’s contribution.</p><p>Research topics. 18.01 Money, credit, and debt relations. 18.02 Banking, maturity transformation, and runs. 18.03 Keynes, effective demand, and uncertainty. 18.04 Monetarism, rational expectations, and policy responses. 18.05 Minsky, leverage, and financial instability. 18.06 Asset bubbles, narratives, and behavioral finance. 18.07 Sovereign debt, international currencies, and financial power. 18.08 Crisis rescues and distributional consequences. 18.09 The financial accelerator, collateral, and balance sheets. 18.10 Household debt and the debt-service ratio DSR. 18.11 Cash flow, maturity mismatch, and credit backstops.</p></div>',1)])])}const m=a(s,[["render",o]]);export{h as __pageData,m as default};
